{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Store-cities.</b> Because everyone engaged in construction becomes impoverished — and the expression מסכן means 'poor.' And one may say: מסכנות — the craftsmen who stand many times in danger atop the building." "<b>Pithom and Raamses.</b> This means: the abyss swallows up the building." "<b>Raamses.</b> One by one it dissolves and collapses. And it is difficult, for it writes בפרך — with a soft mouth. At first Pharaoh said to them: 'To each of you I give [payment] for every brick you make.' And they all came and pressed themselves because the wage was desirable, and they produced more than enough. And once Pharaoh saw this, he said to them: 'Complete your quota of bricks as [you did] when a wage was given to you.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:25.926905617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}